{"content":"{
  "reason": "The TestFlight leg failure is a self-hosted runner infrastructure defect, not a product regression: the registration session matching build-ios's '[self-hosted, macos-m5, fa-m5-1]' pin (added by gh-1692, commit 9de855f1, 2026-10-19 09:33Z) consumes 'Build iOS IPA' job messages and never executes them — jobs sit startedAt-stamped but queued with 0 steps, no runner_name, and no log blob (job-log endpoint returns BlobNotFound). Reproduced live in this session: dispatched build-mobile (none/all) at 06:50Z; the job was delivered (startedAt 06:51:08Z) and sat queued with zero telemetry for 14 minutes until I cancelled the probe run (39557953541). Meanwhile the same physical box served unpinned [self-hosted, macos-m5] jobs normally minutes earlier (runner_name=fa-m5-1, 30 steps, logs). No repository change can execute a job message the runner session never runs; the pin's alternative target (fa-m5-2) has a broken signing env (gh-1692), and migrating the signed iOS lane to hosted macOS runners is an owner cost/quota decision. The gh-172 queue-stall guard and the self-filing issue cycle performed exactly as designed — this issue is the predicted damage PR #1723 flagged ('the physical fa-m5-1 worker itself needs ops attention (reboot/de-register)').",
  "tried": [
    "Correlated all 5 eaten build-ios messages (10-20 x2, 10-21 x2, plus the live probe) against the pin merge: last good build 10-19 05:28 (pre-pin, runner_name=fa-m5-1, 24 steps); 100% eaten since the pin; unpinned macos-m5 jobs healthy throughout",
    "Verified the watcher's queue-stall timings match its design to the second (watch start + 1875s + one poll), i.e. the guard is correct, not a false positive — the job was never in_progress on the API",
    "Verified the three 'failing' jobs in the issue are one root cause: submit-ios and release-mobile were cascade-cancelled by the watcher's run-level containment",
    "Ruled out repo-side routing fixes: removing the pin re-opens the fa-m5-2 silent-archive-failure coin flip; fa-m5-2 itself is broken (unverified signing env); hosted-runner migration is a cost/owner decision; the 90m job timeout-minutes is runner-enforced and can never fire for an eaten message",
    "Live reproduction probe: dispatched build-mobile (android_content=none, ios_content=all) as run 39557953541 at 06:50:34Z; Build iOS IPA delivered at 06:51:08Z then queued with 0 steps / no runner_name for 14 min; cancelled the probe run cleanly (no draft release, no publish — both downstream jobs require build-ios success)",
    "Confirmed the empty digest is a secondary gh-1472-class gap (report job raced GitHub's log-upload lag by 3s; one-shot per-job log fetch with no retry) — cosmetic, not the leg failure"
  ],
  "needs": "Owner/admin action on the fa-m5 boxes: (1) list repo runner registrations and find the stale/wedged session carrying the literal 'fa-m5-1' label (CI token lacks the runners admin permission — GET /actions/runners returns 403); (2) on the physical fa-m5-1 Mac: stop the runner service, de-register ALL registrations, clean RUNNER_TEMP stale-workspace sidecars (gh-160) and check disk, re-register ONE service with explicit labels 'self-hosted,macos-m5,fa-m5-1'; (3) audit fa-m5-2's signing env (10-17/10-18 silent archive failures) or keep it out of the iOS pool; (4) verify with a build-mobile (none/all) dispatch — Build iOS IPA must show steps + runner_name + a growing log within ~2 minutes. Once healthy, the next scheduled daily re-runs the leg and gh-1735 auto-closes; no code change is required."
}
